sment":"PowerShell downloaded and executed an HTA file from the Startup folder, which spawned a cmd.exe process that ran calc.exe. Multiple processes in this chain accessed the LSA registry key, indicating credential enumeration activity.","findings":[{"technique_id":"T1012","name":"Query Registry","parent":null,"tactics":["Discovery"],"behavior":"mshta.exe, cmd.exe, calc.exe, and Calculator.exe accessed HKLM\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa registry to enumerate security credentials.","slot":0,"reasoning":"The processes accessed the LSA registry key with minimal read access (0x1), which is consistent with querying or enumerating registry values rather than modifying them for persistence or credential dumping. This is registry reconnaissance to discover security configuration, not credential extraction or persistence mechanism abuse.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E012","field":"ObjectName","quote":"\\REGISTRY\\MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\ControlSet001\\Control\\Lsa","ok":true},{"event_id":"E012","field":"AccessMask","quote":"0x1","ok":true},{"event_id":"E027","field":"ProcessName","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1218.005","name":"Mshta","parent":"System Binary Proxy Execution","tactics":["Stealth"],"behavior":"PowerShell created and executed T1218.005.hta file from the Startup folder via mshta.exe, which spawned cmd.exe to run calc.exe.","slot":1,"reasoning":"The evidence shows PowerShell directly spawning mshta.exe with a local HTA file path as an argument, which is the core behavior of T1218.005 (System Binary Proxy Execution: Mshta). The subsequent cmd.exe and calc.exe execution are the payload delivered through the HTA file, not the technique itself\u2014the technique is the abuse of mshta.exe as a trusted binary to execute the HTA content.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E005","field":"CommandLine","quote":"\"C:\\windows\\system32\\mshta.exe\" \"C:\\Users\\wardog\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\St